e of reiner he describes reiner as  the weakest in the group  and someone who is basically a butt  kisser with no real talent of his own  after this argument he even punched  reiner in the face  and then on a separate occasion he tried  to punch reiner again  after after rhino was chosen as the  armored titan  his hatred for rhino grew even more once  he discovered many years later  that his brother marcel had died to  protect him from this titan  things eventually came full circle  though as ymir would willingly give the  draw titan back to mali  with porco chosen to be the inheritor  this new draw titan is very similar to  how his brothers used to look  but it could not be any more different  to ymir's one to start with  he has hardened skin covering his face  which offers a degree of protection that  yamir's titan never had  this hardened skin is clearly  bulletproof to an extent as we saw  during episode 1  and his claws also appear longer than  hers used to be as well  this is great for crushing things or  ripping them apart and his arms are just  significantly larger than hers used to  be  as you'd expect the draw of the draw  titan is its main appeal  thanks to porco will get a good look  this season at just how powerful this  draw actually is  as he'll crush things that other titans  simply cannot do  additionally the draw titan is the  swiftest of them all  and can maneuver around at great speeds  that can catch other titans off guard  one interesting thing about porco is  that he is currently  unable to see the memories of his  brother despite inheriting the same  titan  he can however see the memories of ymir  and through her eyes he saw how rhino  was pretending to be the big brother to  all the scouts on the island  it kind of made poco think that reiner  was trying to imitate marcel  and to be honest that pretty much was  the case so yeah  poco is basically right in his  assumption anyway guys  that was the new draw titan explained be  sure to drop a like if you haven't  already  and like i said at the beginning let me  know which topics you'd like to see me  cover  in the future until the next one peace  out
 

